<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 0.77 pct below parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 0.77 pct below parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.3830 to the dollar, down from 3.3250 on Friday and flat at 1.8885 against the mark, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.77 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Friday's 0.20 percent above parity fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
